; Authorized AEGIS lab zone (G0.4c). Every address is from a documentation range
; (RFC 5737 203.0.113.0/24, RFC 3849 2001:db8::/32); nothing here points at a real host.
;
; This file is the zone CoreDNS serves. `deploy/lab/inventory.json` is the same record set in
; machine-readable form, and `scripts/lab/check_inventory.py` fails when the two drift.
; Keep one record per line: the checker parses this file with a deliberately small grammar.

$ORIGIN lab.aegis.test.
$TTL 3600

@   IN SOA ns1.lab.aegis.test. hostmaster.lab.aegis.test. (
        2026112502 ; serial
        3600       ; refresh
        600        ; retry
        604800     ; expire
        300 )      ; negative TTL
    IN NS  ns1.lab.aegis.test.

ns1  IN A    203.0.113.53
www  IN A    203.0.113.10
www  IN AAAA 2001:db8::10
api  IN A    203.0.113.30
mail IN A    203.0.113.20
mail IN MX   10 mx1.lab.aegis.test.
mx1  IN A    203.0.113.25
vpn  IN CNAME www.lab.aegis.test.
txt  IN TXT  "aegis lab zone; not a real domain"
; G1.6a service containers: the lab's own addresses (RFC 1918), reachable only from
; aegis-lab-lab. Ports and images are in deploy/lab/inventory.json (one story).
web   IN A    10.114.53.211
app   IN A    10.114.53.212
ssh   IN A    10.114.53.213
cache IN A    10.114.53.214
httpd IN A    10.114.53.215
